{"data":{"id":"10.48550/arxiv.2509.15031","type":"dois","attributes":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2509.15031","prefix":"10.48550","suffix":"arxiv.2509.15031","identifiers":[{"identifier":"2509.15031","identifierType":"arXiv"}],"alternateIdentifiers":[{"alternateIdentifierType":"arXiv","alternateIdentifier":"2509.15031"}],"creators":[{"name":"Pham, Chau","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Chau","familyName":"Pham","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Dao, Quan","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Quan","familyName":"Dao","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Bhosale, Mahesh","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Mahesh","familyName":"Bhosale","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Tian, Yunjie","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Yunjie","familyName":"Tian","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Metaxas, Dimitris","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Dimitris","familyName":"Metaxas","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Doermann, David","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"David","familyName":"Doermann","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]}],"titles":[{"title":"AutoEdit: Automatic Hyperparameter Tuning for Image Editing"}],"publisher":"arXiv","container":{},"publicationYear":2025,"subjects":[{"lang":"en","subject":"Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (cs.CV)","subjectScheme":"arXiv"},{"subject":"FOS: Computer and information sciences","subjectScheme":"Fields of Science and Technology (FOS)"},{"subject":"FOS: Computer and information sciences","schemeUri":"http://www.oecd.org/science/inno/38235147.pdf","subjectScheme":"Fields of Science and Technology (FOS)"}],"contributors":[],"dates":[{"date":"2025-09-18T14:56:50Z","dateType":"Submitted","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2025-09-19T00:45:11Z","dateType":"Updated","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2025-10-07T15:01:35Z","dateType":"Submitted","dateInformation":"v2"},{"date":"2025-10-08T00:53:27Z","dateType":"Updated","dateInformation":"v2"},{"date":"2025-09","dateType":"Available","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2025","dateType":"Issued"}],"language":null,"types":{"ris":"GEN","bibtex":"misc","citeproc":"article","schemaOrg":"CreativeWork","resourceType":"Article","resourceTypeGeneral":"Preprint"},"relatedIdentifiers":[],"relatedItems":[],"sizes":[],"formats":[],"version":"2","rightsList":[{"rights":"Creative Commons Attribution Non Commercial Share Alike 4.0 International","rightsUri":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/legalcode","schemeUri":"https://spdx.org/licenses/","rightsIdentifier":"cc-by-nc-sa-4.0","rightsIdentifierScheme":"SPDX"}],"descriptions":[{"description":"Recent advances in diffusion models have revolutionized text-guided image editing, yet existing editing methods face critical challenges in hyperparameter identification. To get the reasonable editing performance, these methods often require the user to brute-force tune multiple interdependent hyperparameters, such as inversion timesteps and attention modification. This process incurs high computational costs due to the huge hyperparameter search space. We consider searching optimal editing's hyperparameters as a sequential decision-making task within the diffusion denoising process. Specifically, we propose a reinforcement learning framework, which establishes a Markov Decision Process that dynamically adjusts hyperparameters across denoising steps, integrating editing objectives into a reward function. The method achieves time efficiency through proximal policy optimization while maintaining optimal hyperparameter configurations. Experiments demonstrate significant reduction in search time and computational overhead compared to existing brute-force approaches, advancing the practical deployment of a diffusion-based image editing framework in the real world. Codes can be found at https://github.com/chaupham1709/AutoEdit.git.","descriptionType":"Abstract"},{"description":"Provided code link","descriptionType":"Other"}],"geoLocations":[],"fundingReferences":[]